# Block quotes and dividers of a Markdown (reference/components/markdown.md#block-quotes-and-dividers). Page area of
# 260 × 160 from (20, 20); the lines of text are 12 high.
#
# m1, without rules: the quote has no look of its own, and its paragraph goes like the ones around it; the divider is
#   a line of 0.5 across the whole width, with nothing above or below it.
# m2, inside a Block with Style: custom, whose nested rules change both: the quote has a background, a padding of 4
#   and no line, and holds a paragraph and another quote, which takes the same rule; the divider is a line of 2 with a
#   margin of 4 above and below.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 300
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
		For style: custom
			For element: Block quote
				Box:
					Padding: 4
					Border: 0
					Background: #F1EFE8
			For element: Divider
				Box:
					Border: 2 0 0 0
					Border color: #C00000
					Margin: 4 0
	Section:
		Markdown:
			Id: m1
			Content >>
				Antes.

				> Una cita.

				---

				Después.
		Block:
			Id: b2
			Style: custom
			Box:
				Margin: 10 0 0 0
			Markdown:
				Id: m2
				Content >>
					> Fuera.
					>
					> > Dentro.

					***

					Final.
